  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Cleaned cups are ready for reuse after the café’s normal washing procedure and can be listed as available.\", \"decision\": \"How should cleaned cups rejoin available stock?\", \"goal\": \"Make cup lending and return convenient while keeping the available stock and volunteer work understandable.\", \"problem\": \"A neighborhood café wants to lend reusable cups at community gatherings and recover them afterward. It has a modest cup stock, washable collection crates, a simple lending record, and volunteers who can share short shifts. The plan concerns a small pilot with no deposit or sales system. Different decisions address separate moments in lending, return, and review.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nThe washing and lending volunteers count cleaned cups together during the handover and update one shared list. Both stations agree on the stock change at the same moment.\nThe lending volunteer updates the available-stock list after receiving and counting cleaned cups. Availability reflects stock physically present at the station.\nThe washing volunteer adds cleaned cups to the available-stock list before moving them to the lending station. The lending team can anticipate the incoming supply."
    }
